 1. Introduction
+1. Introduction
+1. Introduction
0  This  document  describes  the  installation,  operation  and maintenance
0                                          ______
+procedures for the Columbia University VM MAILER.    Please  read  sections
0                                              ______
+COPYR  and  TERMS  on  the  terms under which MAILER is provided to you and
0destroy the files that have been provided if you are  unable  to  abide  by
0them.
0
0  Section RESPONS, below, briefly gives a job description for the person or
0                             ______
+persons required to maintain MAILER at your site.  Sections following  that
0                                   ______
+go  into the details of installing MAILER the first time and maintaining it
0and the data it needs to operate on  BITNET.    The  information  in  these
0sections  is written with the assumption that the reader is conversant with
0the basic concepts of VM/SP and RSCS networking.  No  attempt  is  made  to
0define terms.
0
0  ______
+  MAILER  was  developed  by  E.  Alan  Crosswell,  an employee of Columbia
0University in the City of New York.  It is the property of the Trustees  of
0Columbia  University  in  the  City of New York.  Some portions of the code
0                         ______
+have been contributed by MAILER users on  BITNET  (their  names  are  cited
0                             ______
+within  the  source  code).  MAILER is written in IBM 370 Assembly language
0and C.
0
