+2. MAILER Maintainer and Postmaster Job Description
+2. MAILER Maintainer and Postmaster Job Description
+2. MAILER Maintainer and Postmaster Job Description
0  There  are  actually two jobs involved in running a mail service.  One is
0that of maintaining and updating the mail software and  databases  and  the
0other is to perform the duties of Postmaster.
0
0      ______
+  The MAILER maintainer's responsibilities include:
0
                                                                 ______
+   1. Installation   and   configuration   of   the   initial   MAILER
       distribution.
0                                  ______
+   2. Occassional installation of MAILER software  updates  (typically
                                    - 3 -
+
1                    ______
+                    MAILER Installation and Maintenance
0
       on  the  order  of  once  or  twice  a  year  but sometimes more
       frequently).
0   3. Monthly acquisition and installation of the BITNET database used
           ______
+      by  MAILER.    This database is maintained by the BITNET Network
       Information Center (BITNIC) and is distributed monthly over  the
       network   (or  sometimes  by  tape  during  periods  of  network
       instability).  This maintenance is related to the other  monthly
       BITNET node maintenance work (e.g. updating the RSCS DIRECT).
0
 None  of  these  responsibilities  tend  to  be particularly time-consuming
0although it depends on the individual's familiarity with VM and would  best
0be  performed  (or  supervised)  by  a  systems  programmer.   There is the
0                           ______
+potential for an incorrect MAILER installation to crash your VM system  (by
0filling  up  CP  SPOOL  space) or to "clobber" the network (by causing mail
0loops).
0
0  The Postmaster's responsibilities include:
0
    1. Answering local users' questions about the mail system.
0   2. Responding to queries from outsiders (typically requesting  help
       in reaching a particular member of your site's community).
0   3. Diagnosing  miscellaneous  mail  system  errors.    For example,
       ______
+      MAILER sends "error mail" that can't be automatically dealt with
       to the Postmaster.
0
0  The  Postmaster should read his or her mail frequently (many do it one or
0more times daily).  The degree of work involved  in  being  the  Postmaster
0depends  on  how  much  service  you  want to provide to your community and
0outsiders.  For example, you  may  be  willing  to  spend  a  lot  of  time
0answering requests for the electronic address of Professor Smith or you may
0prefer to suggest that the requestor simply call  Professor  Smith  on  the
0telephone to find out her userid.  At Columbia, the daily Postmaster duties
                                    - 4 -
+
1                    ______
+                    MAILER Installation and Maintenance
0
 are peformed by a  trained  student  with  student  training,  back-up  and
0difficult questions handled by a full-time staff member.
0
