 9.1.6. INTERNET
+9.1.6. INTERNET
+9.1.6. INTERNET
0  This  type  1  exit  was  written  by  Henry  Nussbacher  of the Weizmann
0Institute, Rehovot, Israel and is based on the DEFRT exit as  well  as  the
0old  BSMTP exit written by Arthur Ecock of the City University of New York.
0Reg Quinton and Jeffrey Honig have also contributed code to it.    INTERNET
0is  used  in  the  "*DEFAULT*"  position of the Profile OUTGOING table.  It
0searches for host names ending in ".ARPA", ".UUCP", ".DEC", and so  on  and
0routes  via  the appropriate gateway.  Much of INTERNET's capability is now
0                ______
+in the mainline MAILER code (using the DOMAINS table) and  the  BSMTP  exit
0(using the at-sign and percent-preceded parameters).
0
0                                RETURN
+                                RETURN
