 9.3.1. FWDMAIL
+9.3.1. FWDMAIL
+9.3.1. FWDMAIL
0  This exit provides mail forwarding.  The list of recipients to forward to
0must be defined with a variable assignment in the Profile.    The  variable
0name  must  be  8  characters  or  less  and  is  supplied  as the required
0parameter.
0
 9.3.2. RSMAIL
+9.3.2. RSMAIL
+9.3.2. RSMAIL
0  This exit provides mail resending.  This is similar to forwarding and the
0list  of  recipients  is  supplied  in  the  same  way as for FWDMAIL.  The
0difference between the two is that FWDMAIL creates a new mail header  while
0RSMAIL  simply  adds  "Resent-To", "Resent-From", and "Resent-Cc" fields to
0the original header.
0
0  An example of using FWDMAIL or RSMAIL follows:
0
     people=SMITH@CUVMA,JONES@CUVMB
     alan=EACUS@CUVMA
      ...
     SPECIAL:
     CROSSWELL  RSMAIL  1  alan
     FOO-L      RSMAIL  1  people
0
 9.3.3. DISTLIST
+9.3.3. DISTLIST
+9.3.3. DISTLIST
0  DISTLIST uses BSMTP  to  re-distribute  mail  to  a  list  of  recipients
0                           _________
+                           _________
+                           _________
+                          "parameter DISTLIST"
+                          "parameter DISTLIST"
+contained in a file named "parameter DISTLIST".  The file should be RECFM V
0and have one address per line.  This exit does not edit or add anything  to
0the  mail  header  at  all (other than having the side effect of causing an
0additional "Received:" header to be added) and could  be  very  useful  for
0distribution  of  large  mailing lists.  The only restriction on the use of
0this exit is that all the recipients listed must be reachable  with  BSMTP.
0                                  - 22 -
+
1                    ______
+                    MAILER Installation and Maintenance
0
 That is, it must not matter that the recipient's address does not appear in
0the "To:" line of the RFC822 mail.  This restriction is satisfied for LOCAL
0and  DEFRT  distribution  as  well  as  any  mail server that is defined in
0OUTGOING/DOMAINS with the BSMTP exit.  In other words, if  a  recipient  is
0reached with the BITNET exit, then the mail will most likely be returned to
0the sender with an error of "No recipients for this node."
0
0                   "SAMPLE DISTLIST"
+                   "SAMPLE DISTLIST"
+  For a file named "SAMPLE DISTLIST":
0
     SMITH@CUVMA
     JONES@CUVMB
0
0  An example profile entry would be:
0
     SPECIAL:
     SOME-GROUP  DISTLIST 1 SAMPLE
0
