 users via SMSG.  SMSG replies are sent back to the issuer via CP MSGNOH  if
0     ______
+the  MAILER has the necessary privileges.  If not, CP MSG is used.  Help on
0commands may be obtained by use of "?" in commands and  subcommands.    For
0example, "CP SMSG MAILER ?" will cause a list of the valid general commands
0to be sent back.
0
0  Privileged commands are  described  in  "MAILER  HELPPRIV".    These  are
0designed for debugging purposes and to aid general maintenance.
