 11.2. "MAILER PROFILE" updates
+11.2. "MAILER PROFILE" updates
+11.2. "MAILER PROFILE" updates
0       MG
+       MG
+  The  MG  program  can  be  used  to  automate regeneration of your site's
0"MAILER PROFILE" which must usually be done once a month  when  the  latest
0"NAMES"  files  become  available.    Using  MG,  you  only  have  to  make
0                                                   ______
+site-specific changes once, when you first install MAILER.
0
 11.2.1. Files Used by MG
+11.2.1. Files Used by MG
+11.2.1. Files Used by MG
0  MG uses four or more input files:
0
 "* NAMES"             The NAMES files previously described in section 4.
0
  ____                                                        ____
+"name MTPLATE"        The template file used by MG to build "name PROFILE".
                       This  file  looks  just  like  the  Profile  with the
                       exception that the  incoming,  outgoing  and  domains
                                                                  %incoming
+                                                                 %incoming
+                      table  lines  are  replaced  by  the words %incoming,
                       %outgoing     %domains
+                      %outgoing     %domains
+                      %outgoing and %domains, respectively.    MG  replaces
                       these  lines  with  the appropriate information taken
                       from "XMAILER NAMES", "MAILER NAMES", "DOMAIN NAMES",
                                                                    %include
+                            ____                                   %include
+                      and  "name  MAILLCL".    You  can  also use "%include
                       __ __ __
+                      fn.ft.fm" to cause a  file  to  be  included  in  the
                       output Profile.
0
  ____
+"name MAILLCL"        This  file  consists of the lines in the OUTGOING and
                       DOMAINS tables that will be different for your  site.
                       That  is,  the entry or entries for the local system.
                       For example, for the site CUVMB,  the  Outgoing  line
                       for  CUVMB  specifies  the  BITNET  exit in all other
                       sites'  Profiles  and  the  LOCAL  exit  for  CUVMB's
                                             ____
+                      Profile.  Entries in "name MAILLCL" should follow the
                       same syntax as lines  in  the  Outgoing  table.    No
                       comments or blank lines are permitted.
0
0                            MAILER
+  ____                      MAILER
+  Name, above, is typically MAILER, but you may use any convenient name.
0
