 11.2.2. Invoking MG
+11.2.2. Invoking MG
+11.2.2. Invoking MG
0  To run MG, type:
0
             ____  _________ _____ ____ _____
+    MG [-i] name [alternate NAMES file names]
0
 _____
+NAMES file names preceded by a "-d" are used for the DOMAINS table.  Others
0are used for the OUTGOING and INCOMING tables.
0
0  The typical invocation of MG is:
0
     MG MAILER
0
0  An example of using a different Outgoing/Incoming NAMES file is:
0
     MG MAILER NEWBIT.NAMES.G MAILER.NAMES
0
0  Finally, an example of using a different DOMAINS NAMES file is:
0
     MG MAILER -d NEWDOM.NAMES
0
 [Note the use of OS-style "dot" notation for file names.]
0
0  You will normally not need the "-i" switch to MG which tells it to set up
0an  "initial  distribution" profile -- that is, a profile for a Mailer that
0other Mailers do not yet have in their INCOMING tables.  The  default  list
0of   NAMES   files   used   by  MG  is:    "XMAILER.NAMES  MAILER.NAMES  -d
0DOMAIN.NAMES".
0
0  MG will also accept EARN-style "NODES" files which differ  only  slightly
0                                  - 27 -
+
1                    ______
+                    MAILER Installation and Maintenance
0
 from  the  BITNET  "NAMES"  files.   So, if you prefer to use the EARN node
0administration tools, you may do so.
0
